                <pb facs="0195" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.G1/154a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-22T23:00:00-04:00">May 22, 1943—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>345. Your 500, May 21, 7 p.m. Department approves your action in postponing
                    presentation of question to Soviet Government in view of British Ambassador’s
                    statements, and will consult British Government again and send you new
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
